3. CLEAN-ROOM & ZERO THIRD-PARTY RUNTIME DEPENDENCY ATTESTATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

lh-navic-decoder is a 100% clean-room implementation written by Sameer Tawade at
Logihertz Systems (OPC) Private Limited.

  * Zero External Runtime Dependencies: All core parsers, mathematical engines,
    cryptographic/signal-processing primitives, rule evaluators, and SARIF
    exporters are implemented strictly using the native ISO C++17 Standard Library (g++ / clang++)
    standard library.
  * Supply-Chain Provenance: This package embeds zero third-party vendor code
    fragments, zero external runtime packages, and zero telemetry beacons,
    enabling deterministic, offline, air-gapped verification and deployment.

